  "index_test": "whole-animal-in-vivo",
  "index_test_evidence": "The main aim of this project was to examine the strengths and weaknesses of animal studies to predict human toxicity (HT). The database was developed from a survey which covered only those compounds where HTs were identified during clinical development of new pharmaceuticals, determining whether animal toxicity studies identified concordant target organ toxicities in humans.",
  "decision": "include",
  "reason": "The study reports quantitative measures of concordance (e.g., \"true positive HT concordance rate of 71% for rodent and nonrodent species\") between animal toxicity studies and human clinical toxicity for pharmaceuticals. The index test is whole-animal-in-vivo."
